error[V0311]: `name_of` is an async function, so it cannot return part of `user`; return a copy instead, with `.clone()`
 --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0311_async_returns_part/main.vr:6:5
  |
6 |     user.name
  |     ^^^^^^^^^ `name_of` is an async function, so it cannot return part of `user`; return a copy instead, with `.clone()`
  |
  = note: every value an async function returns must be new, since it is handed over after the function has stopped and started again
  = note: in Rust terms, the returned future would borrow its arguments, which Varyk does not support
help: insert `.clone()` after `name`
